      en: "The Anabar Plateau is located in northern Siberia, east of the Lena River mouth. It is a highland with elevations between 400 and 700 m, reaching up to about 905 m. The plateau consists of Precambrian rocks, mainly granites and gneisses, heavily dissected by rivers. Major rivers are the Anabar and Popigai. Vegetation is boreal coniferous forest (taiga) in the south and forest-tundra in the north. The climate is subarctic, with long, cold winters (-30 °C) and short, mild summers (+12 °C). The area is rich in diamond deposits, occurring in kimberlite pipes. Population density is extremely low, mainly Dolgans and Evenks.",
